---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Turf — Privacy, cookies, and analytics';
const description =
  'What turf.build collects, which cookies we set once you accept them, and how to change your mind or ask us to delete your data.';
---

<Layout title={title} description={description}>
  <section class="subhero">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow"><span class="dot"></span> Privacy</p>
      <h1>What this site collects.</h1>
      <p class="lede">turf.build is a static site. There is no account to create, no backend, and no
        analytics or advertising cookie until you accept them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h3>Cookies and consent</h3>
      <p>When you first visit, a banner asks whether we may set measurement cookies. Until you
        choose <em>Accept</em>, no analytics or advertising script is loaded at all. If you choose
        <em>Decline</em>, none is ever loaded. Your choice is stored in your browser under
        <code>turf.consent</code> — it never leaves your device.</p>
      <p>To change your answer, use <strong>Cookie settings</strong> at the bottom of any page, or
        clear this site's storage in your browser.</p>

      <h3>What loads after you accept</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Google Analytics</strong> (property <code>G-HYNQ83NRR2</code>) — page views and
          referrers, so we know which pages are useful. IP addresses are handled by Google; see the
          <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google privacy policy</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>LinkedIn Insight Tag</strong> (partner <code>9817980</code>) — tells us when a
          visit followed one of our LinkedIn posts or ads. See LinkedIn's
          <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/legal/cookie-policy">cookie policy</a>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We use both for aggregate measurement. We do not sell data, and we do not combine it with
        anything else to identify you personally.</p>

      <h3>What you give us directly</h3>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Newsletter</strong> — the footer form posts your email address to
          <a href="https://buttondown.com/">Buttondown</a>, which stores it until you unsubscribe.
          Every message carries an unsubscribe link.</li>
        <li><strong>Email</strong> — anything you send to <a href="mailto:contact@turf.build">contact@turf.build</a>
          lands in our inbox and stays there while we're in touch.</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Hosting</h3>
      <p>The site is served by GitHub Pages, which records standard request logs including IP
        addresses. That happens at the network level, before any page of ours runs, and is covered by
        the <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub
        privacy statement</a>.</p>

      <h3>Your data</h3>
      <p>To ask what we hold, to correct it, or to have it deleted, email
        <a href="mailto:contact@turf.build?subject=Privacy%20request">contact@turf.build</a>. Say
        which email address to look for and we'll confirm when it's done.</p>
      <p>Nothing here covers the Turf CLI itself, which runs on your machine against your own cloud
        credentials.</p>

      <h3>Changes</h3>
      <p>If this policy changes materially, we'll update the date below and note it in the release
        notes.</p>
      <p><em>Effective 17 August 2026.</em></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
